# Frontend React Patterns

## Component Structure

- **Function components** with **default exports**, one per file
- Feature components live flat in `components/`; reusable UI primitives in `components/ui/`
- **Keep files under ~350 lines**. If a component grows beyond that, extract sub-views or form sections into sibling files
- Animation: `framer-motion` (`motion.div` with `initial`/`animate`/`transition`)
- Icons: `lucide-react`
- DnD: `@dnd-kit`

## Tailwind CSS Design Tokens

Tokens are defined in `index.css` via `@theme { ... }`. Always use token classes, never raw hex:

```
bg-surface-0  bg-surface-1  bg-surface-2  bg-surface-3  bg-surface-4
text-text-primary  text-text-secondary  text-text-tertiary
border-border-subtle  border-border-default  border-border-strong
text-accent  bg-accent  text-success  text-warning  text-danger
```

Common patterns: `rounded-xl`, fractional opacity `bg-accent/[0.03]`, conditional classes via template literals. Supports `[data-theme="light"]` via same CSS variable names.

## Dropdowns / Selects

Never use native `<select>`. Use the custom dropdown pattern (`FormSelect` in `ui/FormSelect.tsx` for forms, or the `Dropdown` pattern in `FilterToolbar.tsx` for toolbars): trigger button with `ChevronDown`, `AnimatePresence` + `motion.div` popover, click-outside dismiss.

## Form Input Styling

Standard input class string (consistent across all forms):

```
w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-border-default bg-surface-2 text-sm text-text-primary placeholder:text-text-quaternary focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-accent/50
```

## Modal Pattern

Modals follow this structure: fixed backdrop (`bg-black/50`), `motion.div` container with `rounded-2xl bg-surface-1 border border-border-default shadow-2xl`, header with icon + title + X close button, optional error banner, scrollable body, footer with actions.

## Zustand Stores

- One `create<StateInterface>()` call per store; **`useWorkspaceStore`** is composed in `stores/workspace/index.ts` from `slices/*` (core, tasks, chat, logs, workflow, requirements) — import still `from '../stores/workspace'`.
- Naming: `useWorkspaceStore`, `useUIStore`, `useI18nStore`
- Action naming conventions:
  - `fetch*` / `refresh*` — server sync
  - `set*` — simple state setters
  - `add*` / `remove*` / `update*` — CRUD operations
  - `send*` / `send*Stream` — API calls with optional SSE
  - `run*` — workflow execution
  - `toggle*` / `open*` / `close*` — UI state
  - `patch*` — partial server-shaped updates
- Access specific slices with selectors: `useWorkspaceStore((s) => s.activeWorkspaceId)`

## Types

All TypeScript types live in `types/index.ts` as a single barrel. String union types mirror backend domain vocabulary. Use `as const` arrays with derived union types for constrained pick-lists.
